  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be the set of positive integral values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></math>. Then, the number of elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is:",
